  "as_of": "2010-11-24",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would expand scrutiny of foreign agricultural land acquisitions, put national interest criteria into legislation and require public information about proposed investments.",
   "It would require applications to the Treasurer for covered foreign interests in agricultural land larger than 5 hectares, regardless of the purchase price.",
   "The bill would cover land mainly used for primary production businesses, with acquisition exceptions for wills, loan security and transfers from specified public bodies."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The Treasurer could prohibit proposed acquisitions exceeding 5 hectares where they would be contrary to the national interest.",
   "The Treasurer could order a foreign person to dispose of an interest acquired contrary to the national interest.",
   "National interest decisions would have to consider security, competition, tax revenue, effects on the economy or community, and the investor's character.",
   "Online disclosures would identify investors, residence or business location, investment amounts and agricultural sectors, with information updated as applications progress.",
   "A foreign person entering a covered acquisition agreement without first notifying the Treasurer would face an offence punishable by a fine or imprisonment."
  ],
  "affected": "Foreign investors acquiring interests in Australian agricultural land and the Treasurer are affected.",
